    \node[pin=90:{$y_4$}] at (axis cs:2,0) {};

    % Shaded region
    \addplot[domain=-2:2, samples=100, fill=red!30, fill opacity=0.5] {0.5*x + 1};
    \addplot[domain=-2:2, samples=100, fill=red!30, fill opacity=0.5] {0.5*x - 1};

    % Dashed lines
    \draw[dashed, gray] (axis cs:0,0) -- (axis cs:0,2);
    \draw[dashed, gray] (axis cs:0,0) -- (axis cs:2,0);

    % Legend
    \legend{$x$, $y_1$, $y_2$, $y_3$, $y_4$}
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{document}
```

This code will create a 2D plot with the specified points and shaded region, along with axis-parallel dashed lines through the point $x$. The plot is designed to be professional and suitable for inclusion in a printed book.

